.TH MONSTAR 5 "2026-07-14" "monstar" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
monstar \- configuration and theme file format
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B monstar
reads configuration from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/monstar/config
or, when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset, from
.IR $HOME/.config/monstar/config .
An alternate file may be selected with
.BR monstar (1)'s
.B \-\-config
option.
A missing or unreadable file produces the default configuration.
.SH TERMINAL COMPATIBILITY
Monstar uses Ghostty's
.B libghostty-vt
terminal core and identifies itself through its installed
.B monstar
terminfo entry.
.SH SYNTAX
The file contains one
.I key = value
entry per line.
Leading and trailing horizontal whitespace is ignored.
Empty lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is
.B #
are comments.
Unknown keys, malformed lines, and invalid values are reported and ignored;
the previous value or default remains in effect.
.PP
For example:
.EX
copy-highlight-duration = 200
font-family = Iosevka
font-size = 12.5
theme = light:Rose Pine Dawn,dark:Rose Pine
window-padding-x = 4,8
.EE
.SH RELOADING
Press
.B Ctrl+Shift+,
or send
.B SIGUSR1
to reload the configuration.
Overrides supplied with
.B \-o
are reapplied after the file is loaded.
.PP
Visual and interaction settings apply to the running window.
The
.BR command ,
.BR env ,
.BR linux-cgroup ,
.BR scrollback-limit ,
and
.B term
settings describe resources created at startup and do not replace or move an
existing child or resize existing scrollback storage.
.SH GENERAL SETTINGS
.TP
.BI app-id " = string"
Set the Wayland app-id and desktop-entry hint.
The default is
.BR dev.rockorager.monstar .
.TP
.BI command " = command"
Set the child command used when no command is supplied on the command line.
An unprefixed value, or one prefixed with
.BR shell: ,
is passed to
.BR /bin/sh " " \-c .
A value prefixed with
.B direct:
is split on spaces and tabs and executed directly; shell quoting is not
interpreted in direct mode.
When unset,
.B SHELL
and then
.B /bin/sh
are used.
.TP
.BI env " = NAME=value"
Set an environment variable for the child.
Repeat this setting for more variables; a later entry for the same name
replaces an earlier one.
An empty value, as in
.BR "env = NAME=" ,
removes the variable from the inherited environment.
Entries apply after Monstar sets
.BR TERM ,
.BR COLORTERM ,
and
.BR PWD ,
so they can replace those too.
Like
.BR command ,
this only affects children started afterwards.
.TP
.BI linux-cgroup " = never|always"
Choose whether each newly spawned child is moved into a separate transient
systemd scope.
The default is
.BR never .
With
.BR always ,
Monstar falls back to its inherited cgroup if the session bus or systemd scope
creation is unavailable.
.TP
.BI pipe-command-output " = command"
Set a shell command that receives the last OSC 133-delimited command output on
standard input when
.B Ctrl+Shift+G
is pressed.
The default is unset.
.TP
.BI term " = name"
Set the
.B TERM
environment variable for the child.
The default is
.BR monstar ,
which names the installed terminfo entry.
Other values should name an entry known on every system the child reaches,
for example over SSH.
.TP
.BI title " = string"
Set a fixed window title.
While set, title changes requested by programs with OSC 0 or OSC 2 are
ignored.
The
.B \-\-title
option only sets the initial title and is overridden by this setting.
.TP
.BI working-directory " = path"
Start the child in
.IR path ,
which must be absolute,
.BR ~ ,
or begin with
.BR ~/ .
When unset, the child inherits Monstar's working directory.
If the directory cannot be used, Monstar warns and inherits its own directory.
The
.B \-\-working-directory
option overrides this setting, and windows opened with
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
start in the current terminal directory instead.
.SH COMMAND COMPLETION NOTIFICATIONS
The shell must emit OSC 133 C/D command-start/end markers. Monstar does not
automatically inject shell integration. These settings do not affect explicit
OSC 9/777 desktop notifications.
.TP
.BI notify-on-command-finish " = never|unfocused|always"
Choose when completed commands can notify. The default is
.BR never .
With
.BR unfocused ,
focus is checked when the command finishes. Alternate-screen use does not
cancel timing, so an editor session can notify when it exits.
.TP
.BI notify-on-command-finish-action " = actions"
Comma-separated
.B bell
and
.B notify
flags, optionally prefixed with
.BR no- .
Each assignment starts from the default: bell enabled, desktop notification
disabled. For desktop notifications only, use
.BR no-bell,notify .
The bell uses the compositor's optional system-bell protocol; desktop
notifications require D-Bus and a notification service.
.TP
.BI notify-on-command-finish-after " = duration"
Notify only when command duration strictly exceeds this value. The default is
.BR 5s .
Use nonnegative integers followed immediately by
.BR y , w , d , h , m , s , ms , us , "µs" ,
or
.BR ns .
Components may be combined, such as
.B 1m30s
or
.BR "1s 250ms" .
A bare
.B 0
disables the minimum duration; fractional numbers are not accepted.
Values saturate at the maximum unsigned 64-bit count of nanoseconds.
.SH FONT SETTINGS
.TP
.BI font-family " = family"
Set the primary font family requested from fontconfig.
The default is
.BR monospace .
Define a virtual family in the user's Fontconfig configuration to provide
ordered primary, styled, and fallback fonts specific to Monstar, then select it
with this setting.
.TP
.BI font-size " = size[pt|px]"
Set the font size.
Bare values and
.B pt
values are typographic points;
.B px
values are logical pixels before Wayland output scaling.
Fractional values greater than zero and no greater than 512 are accepted.
The default is
.BR 12pt ,
equivalent to 16 logical pixels at 96 DPI.
.TP
.BI adjust-cell-height " = pixels|percent%"
Adjust the height derived from the font metrics.
A signed integer adds or removes physical pixels; a percentage scales the
natural height.
For example,
.B 2
adds two pixels,
.B -2
removes two pixels, and
.B 20%
increases the natural height by twenty percent.
The result is at least one pixel, and glyphs remain vertically centered.
Pixel adjustments stay fixed while zooming or changing output scale;
percentage adjustments follow the font metrics.
By default no adjustment is applied.
.SH WINDOW SETTINGS
.TP
.BI background-opacity " = opacity"
Set the opacity of cells using the default terminal background.
The value is between 0 and 1 inclusive; the default is 1.
By default, explicit cell backgrounds, selections, cursors, text, and terminal
graphics retain their own opacity.
.TP
.BI background-blur " = boolean"
Request compositor-provided blur behind a translucent terminal background.
The default is true.
Blur is requested only when
.B background-opacity
is less than 1 and the compositor supports the ext-background-effect-v1
protocol or, as on KDE Plasma, KWin's org_kde_kwin_blur protocol.
.TP
.BI background-opacity-cells " = boolean"
Apply
.B background-opacity
to explicit cell background colors too.
The default is false.
Selections, cursors, text, and terminal graphics retain their own opacity.
.TP
.BI window-padding-x " = pixels[,pixels]"
Set minimum left and right padding in logical pixels.
One value applies to both sides; two values set left and right independently.
The default is zero.
.TP
.BI window-padding-y " = pixels[,pixels]"
Set minimum top and bottom padding in logical pixels.
One value applies to both sides; two values set top and bottom independently.
The default is zero.
.TP
.BI window-height " = rows"
Set the initial terminal grid height in cells.
Takes effect only together with
.BR window-width .
The default is zero, which leaves the size unset.
Values below 4 are raised to 4.
.TP
.BI window-width " = columns"
Set the initial terminal grid width in cells.
Takes effect only together with
.BR window-height .
The default is zero, which leaves the size unset.
Values below 10 are raised to 10.
.B \-\-window-size-chars
sets both settings, and
.B \-\-window-size-pixels
takes precedence over them.
Reloading does not resize an existing window.
.SH CURSOR SETTINGS
.TP
.BI cursor-style " = block|bar|underline|block_hollow"
Set the default cursor shape.
The default is
.BR block .
Programs may select another shape with DECSCUSR; the configured shape returns
when a program requests the default shape or resets the terminal.
Without keyboard focus the cursor is always drawn as a hollow block.
.TP
.BI cursor-style-blink " = true|false"
Choose whether the default cursor blinks while the window has keyboard focus.
The default is
.BR false .
Programs may still request a blinking or steady cursor with DECSCUSR or DEC
private mode 12.
Typing restarts the visible phase, and unfocused windows never blink.
.SH STORAGE AND INPUT SETTINGS
.TP
.BI copy-highlight-duration " = milliseconds"
Set how long copied selections flash.
The default is 200 milliseconds.
Zero disables the flash.
.TP
.BI clipboard-trim-trailing-spaces " = true|false"
Remove trailing whitespace from each line of copied selections.
The default is
.BR true .
.TP
.BI copy-on-select " = true|false|clipboard"
Choose where a finished mouse selection is copied.
.B true
claims the primary selection,
.B clipboard
claims both the primary selection and the clipboard, and
.B false
copies nothing until
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
is pressed.
The default is
.BR true .
.TP
.BI image-storage-limit " = bytes"
Set the kitty graphics image-data limit per terminal screen.
The default is 320000000 bytes and the maximum is 4294967295.
Zero disables the kitty graphics protocol.
.TP
.BI inertial-scrolling " = true|false"
Choose whether precision-device scrolling continues with inertial motion after
the fingers are lifted.
The default is
.BR true .
.TP
.BI mouse-hide-while-typing " = true|false"
Hide the mouse pointer when a key press sends input to the terminal.
Moving the pointer or pressing a button shows it again.
The default is
.BR false .
.TP
.BI mouse-scroll-multiplier " = multiplier"
Apply one multiplier to both precision-device and discrete-wheel scrolling.
Finite values are clamped to the range 0.01 through 10000.
.TP
.BI mouse-scroll-multiplier " = precision:value,discrete:value"
Set the two scrolling multipliers independently.
Either named component may be updated without changing the other.
The defaults are
.B precision:1
and
.BR discrete:3 .
.TP
.BI keybind " = trigger=action"
Add or replace a Ghostty-style single-key binding. Repeat this setting to bind
multiple triggers. Repeating the same trigger replaces its previous binding;
an invalid entry leaves previous bindings unchanged.
.B scroll_page_lines:N
scrolls by N terminal lines: negative values scroll up, positive values scroll
down, and zero consumes the key without moving. N must be between -32768 and
32767.
.B unbind
removes a shortcut and passes its input to the application.
.PP
The default line-scrolling bindings are:
.nf
keybind = shift+up=scroll_page_lines:-1
keybind = shift+down=scroll_page_lines:1
.fi
.PP
For example, add a five-line shortcut and remove the default up shortcut:
.nf
keybind = ctrl+shift+k=scroll_page_lines:-5
keybind = shift+up=unbind
.fi
.PP
Triggers accept lowercase
.BR shift ,
.B ctrl
(alias
.BR control ),
.B alt
(aliases
.BR opt ", " option ),
or
.B super
(aliases
.BR cmd ", " command )
with one key. A single Unicode character follows the keyboard layout;
key names such as
.BR KeyK ", " arrow_up ", " PageUp ", " equal
select physical keys. The aliases
.BR up ", " down ", " left ", " right
are also accepted. Modifiers match exactly, ignoring lock keys and modifier
sides. Include Shift when held to produce punctuation; on a US keyboard,
.B ctrl+shift++=scroll_page_lines:-5
binds Ctrl+Shift+Plus. Use
.B ctrl+==scroll_page_lines:-5
to bind Ctrl+Equals.
.PP
Configured bindings take priority over fixed shortcuts and apply immediately
on configuration reload. Scroll actions pass through on the alternate screen.
Search mode retains its own controls. Supported actions are
.BR scroll_page_lines ,
.BR new_window ,
.BR unbind ,
and the Ghostty tab and split actions
.BR new_tab ,
.BR close_tab ,
.BR close_surface ,
.BR previous_tab ,
.BR next_tab ,
.BR last_tab ,
.BI goto_tab: N\fR,\fP
.BI move_tab: N\fR,\fP
.BI new_split: right|down|left|up\fR,\fP
.BI goto_split: previous|next|up|down|left|right\fR,\fP
.BR toggle_split_zoom ,
.BI resize_split: direction , pixels\fR,\fP
and
.BR equalize_splits .
Tab and split actions are performed by a hosting application such as
.BR monstar-qt ;
in a standalone window their triggers behave as if unbound.
Their defaults follow Ghostty on Linux, for example
.B ctrl+shift+t=new_tab
and
.BR ctrl+shift+o=new_split:right .
Sequences, binding flags and other Ghostty actions are not supported.
.TP
.BI scrollback-limit " = bytes"
Set the terminal page-storage limit, including the active screen.
The default is 50000000 bytes.
.SH QT FRONTEND SETTINGS
These settings are read by
.BR monstar-qt ,
which shows terminals as tabs of splits.
Terminals accept and ignore them.
.TP
.BI window-decoration " = auto|client|server|none"
.B client
replaces the desktop's title bar with one drawn by
.BR monstar-qt ,
holding the icon, the tabs when
.B qt-tabs-location
is
.BR top ,
a new-tab button, and minimize, maximize, and close buttons.
.B none
removes the title bar entirely.
.B auto
and
.B server
keep the desktop's title bar.
The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.BI qt-tabs-location " = top|bottom|left|right"
Choose the window edge for the tab strip.
The default is
.BR top .
.TP
.BI window-show-tab-bar " = always|auto|never"
Choose when the tab strip is shown;
.B auto
shows it with two or more tabs.
The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.BI unfocused-split-opacity " = opacity"
Set the opacity of splits without keyboard focus, from 0.15 to 1.
The default is 0.7.
.TP
.BI unfocused-split-fill " = color"
Set the color laid over unfocused splits.
The default is the
.B background
color.
.TP
.BI split-divider-color " = color"
Set the color of the line between splits.
The default is
.BR 3a3a3a .
.TP
.BI focus-follows-mouse " = true|false"
Focus the split under the pointer.
The default is
.BR false .
.TP
.BI window-inherit-working-directory " = true|false"
Start new tabs, splits, and windows in the focused terminal's directory,
from OSC 7 when the shell reports it.
The default is
.BR true .
.TP
.BI qt-terminal-command " = path"
Run this
.B monstar
executable for each pane.
By default the one installed beside
.B monstar-qt
is used, then the one found on
.BR PATH .
.SH THEME SELECTION
.TP
.BI theme " = name"
Use one named theme in both light and dark desktop color schemes.
.TP
.BI theme " = light:name,dark:name"
Use separate named themes and follow the desktop color-scheme portal.
Both sides are required.
.PP
An absolute theme path is read directly.
A theme name cannot contain path separators and is searched in this order:
.IP 1. 3
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/monstar/themes/name
or
.IR $HOME/.config/monstar/themes/name .
.IP 2. 3
.I $MONSTAR_RESOURCES_DIR/themes/name
when
.B MONSTAR_RESOURCES_DIR
is set.
.IP 3. 3
The installed
.I share/monstar/themes/name
directory relative to the Monstar executable.
.PP
Monstar installs Ghostty's iTerm2 theme collection.
Without a
.B theme
setting, the built-in Fluent 2-based light and dark themes follow the desktop
color scheme.
.SH COLOR SETTINGS
Colors use six hexadecimal RGB digits, with an optional leading
.BR # .
For example,
.B #ffe629
and
.B ffe629
are equivalent.
.B cursor-color
and
.B cursor-text
also accept
.B cell-foreground
and
.B cell-background
to match the cursor cell's colors at runtime.
.PP
An explicit color in the main configuration overrides the named theme.
Runtime OSC color changes may override terminal, cursor, and selection colors
until they are reset by the application.
.TP
.BI background " = color"
Set the default terminal background.
Built-in defaults are
.B #ffffff
in light mode and
.B #292929
in dark mode.
.TP
.BI copy-highlight " = color"
Set the temporary background shown after a selection is copied.
The built-in default is Fluent Yellow Tint 20,
.BR #fdea3d ,
in both color schemes.
.TP
.BI copy-highlight-foreground " = color"
Set text shown during the post-copy flash.
The built-in default is
.B #242424
in both color schemes.
.TP
.BI cursor-color " = color"
Set the cursor color.
A direct color uses six hexadecimal RGB digits, with an optional leading
.BR # .
The special values
.B cell-foreground
and
.B cell-background
match the cursor cell's foreground or background, after reverse video.
An OSC 12 cursor color from the application overrides this until it is reset.
Built-in defaults are
.B #242424
in light mode and
.B #ffffff
in dark mode.
.TP
.BI cursor-text " = color"
Set text beneath a focused block cursor.
Accepts the same values as
.BR cursor-color .
When unset, the terminal background is used.
The usual pairing with
.B cursor-color = cell-foreground
is
.BR "cursor-text = cell-background" .
.TP
.BI foreground " = color"
Set the default terminal foreground.
Built-in defaults are
.B #242424
in light mode and
.B #ffffff
in dark mode.
.TP
.BI palette " = index=color"
Override one terminal palette entry.
The index must be between 0 and 255 and may use decimal or a
.BR 0b ,
.BR 0o ,
or
.B 0x
numeric prefix.
Repeat the setting to override multiple entries.
.TP
.BI selection-background " = color"
Set the selection background.
Built-in defaults are
.B #cfe4fa
in light mode and
.B #0f6cbd
in dark mode.
.TP
.BI selection-foreground " = color"
Set selected text.
Built-in defaults are
.B #242424
in light mode and
.B #ffffff
in dark mode.
.SH THEME FILES
Theme files use the same line syntax as the main configuration but accept only
these color keys:
.BR background ,
.BR copy-highlight ,
.BR copy-highlight-foreground ,
.BR cursor-color ,
.BR cursor-text ,
.BR foreground ,
.BR palette ,
.BR selection-background ,
and
.BR selection-foreground .
The
.B palette
key may be repeated.
.PP
Main-configuration colors override theme-file colors.
Palette entries not supplied by either use the built-in palette.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Fallback base directory when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
.TP
.B MONSTAR_RESOURCES_DIR
Resource directory searched for installed themes.
.TP
.B SHELL
Default child command when
.B command
is unset.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the default configuration and user themes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/monstar/config
Fallback configuration file.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/monstar/themes/
Fallback user theme directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/monstar/config
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/monstar/themes/
User theme directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fontconfig/conf.d/50-monstar.conf
Optional per-user virtual family definition for Monstar-specific font
preferences.
.TP
.I share/doc/monstar/examples/50-monstar.conf
Annotated Fontconfig template, relative to the installation prefix.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR monstar (1)
